From a00f1cf1573784c649c5c50790ec4e9fd9f56290 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cdeletre <cyril.deletre@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:46:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] native: no ErrorLog intro line on the way out

The original writes "Coop vX.Y" and a time stamp to each of its log files
when it closes them. The port sends ErrorLog to the console, so the native
build printed four of these banners at every exit (one per global ErrorLog),
which only clutter the console log. Under GTA2_PORT_NATIVE the destructor
skips them; the web build is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/error.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/error.cpp b/Source/error.cpp
index 2e3fa8f0..c5027c59 100644
--- a/Source/error.cpp
+++ b/Source/error.cpp
@@ -122,7 +122,9 @@ void* ErrorLog::log_on_line_written_4D9670(TLogLineCallback pCallBack)
 MATCH_FUNC(0x4A3610)
 ErrorLog::~ErrorLog()
 {
+#if !defined(GTA2_PORT_NATIVE)
     log_intro_4D95A0();
+#endif
 #if !defined(__clang__) && (_MSC_VER <= 1200)
     field_0_ofstr.close();
 #endif
